# MyColors Architecture

This is a Laravel 12 REST API assessment: E-Commerce Order & Promotion API.

## Mandatory patterns

- **Modular**: domain code lives in `Modules/{Auth,Product,Cart,Promotion,Order}`.
- **Repository pattern**: controllers never query Eloquent directly for business reads/writes.
- **Service layer**: business rules (checkout, discounts, stock) live in Services, not controllers.
- **Clean code**: small methods, explicit names, no god classes, no duplicated logic.

## Layer flow

```
Route → FormRequest → Controller → Service → Repository → Model
                         ↓
                    API Resource / JsonResponse
```

- Controllers: HTTP only (status codes, resources, calling services).
- Services: use-cases, transactions, domain rules.
- Repositories: persistence only (queries, locks, inserts/updates).
- Models: relations, casts, scopes — no checkout/cart business logic.

## Module layout

```
Modules/{Name}/
  app/Http/Controllers|Requests|Resources
  app/Models|Enums|Services|Repositories
  app/Providers
  database/migrations|factories|seeders
  routes/api.php
  tests/Feature|Unit
```

Do not put domain logic in `app/` except shared API base classes (`App\Http\Controllers\Api\BaseController`).

## Cross-module rules

- Prefer interfaces/contracts for repositories bound in the module ServiceProvider.
- Order/Cart may depend on Product/Promotion via repository interfaces — never reach into another module's private internals casually.
- Keep modules API-only (no web views/assets unless explicitly required).

## Do / Don't

```php
// ❌ BAD — fat controller + direct Eloquent
public function store(Request $request) {
    $product = Product::find($request->product_id);
    if ($product->stock_quantity < $request->qty) abort(400);
    CartItem::create([...]);
}

// ✅ GOOD — thin controller
public function store(AddCartItemRequest $request) {
    $item = $this->cartService->addItem($request->user(), $request->validated());
    return $this->success(new CartItemResource($item), 'Item added', 201);
}
```
